# AIRCRAFT-CAPABILITY BENCH parameter set (2026-11-26, owner: "先有一个几乎完美的飞机设置，再考虑飞路径").
# This is NOT a delivered acceptance arm: it is the firmware side of the speed ladder, flown on the open
# 30 m-square bench world with position-only targets (PLANNER=rectangle) so the planner cannot mask or
# cause what the airframe does.
#
# SITL airframe it must match (libraries/SITL/SIM_Frame.h defaults, quad X, mass 3.0 kg):
#   hoverThrOut 0.39, propExpo 0.65, spin 0.15-0.95, slew 150, disc_area 0.385  ->  T/W ~= 4.2
#   => 8-10 m/s is inside the airframe's envelope; the firmware limits below are what cap it today.
#
# GUIDED kinematic limits (mode_guided.cpp: pva_control_start reads WP_SPD/WP_ACC):
WP_SPD       8.0     # was 1.5: horizontal target speed of the position controller's reference model
WP_ACC       8.0     # was 4.0: its acceleration limit; 0.8 g lateral, must stay < g*tan(ATC_ANGLE_MAX)
WP_JERK      30.0    # was 1.0; use only in position-only nav (PVA path uses PSC_NE_JERK)
WP_RADIUS_M  0.5
# attitude envelope: g*tan(55 deg) = 14.0 m/s^2 lateral capability
ATC_ANGLE_MAX 55.0
ATC_ANG_RLL_P 10.0
ATC_ANG_PIT_P 10.0
ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.16
ATC_RAT_RLL_I 0.16
ATC_RAT_RLL_D 0.005
ATC_RAT_PIT_P 0.16
ATC_RAT_PIT_I 0.16
ATC_RAT_PIT_D 0.005
ATC_RAT_YAW_P 0.35
ATC_RAT_YAW_I 0.035
# horizontal position/velocity loop (4.7 names): stiffer than the 1.35 m/s arm, jerk limit high enough that
# the PSC_NE_JERK-derived k_v = jerk/accel stays in a sane 15-25 1/s band
PSC_NE_POS_P 2.0
PSC_NE_VEL_P 2.5
PSC_NE_VEL_I 1.2
PSC_NE_VEL_D 0.25
PSC_NE_JERK 120.0
# motor model consistency with SITL (mismatch makes the acceleration feedforward lie)
MOT_THST_HOVER 0.39
MOT_THST_EXPO 0.65
